; bfsodium SHA3_224 : FIPS 202's SHA3_224  the sponge at rate 144 with pad 6
;
; HAND WRITTEN; The sponge over keccak/permute1600 at this function's own rate;
; The permutation is PASTED and entered once per block of the padded message
; and never again  because twenty eight bytes of digest fit inside one rate;
;
; INTERFACE entry=1 exit=0 footprint=0:1028
; IO  in:  mlen{2} LE  then mlen bytes from the wire
;     out: digest{28}
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x0c7  S{200}  the sponge state; it starts at NOUGHT  which is why
;                         the two length bytes are moved up out of it below
;   @0x0c8:0x330  keccak/permute1600's frame  pasted at this file's own zero
;   @0x338:0x3c7  BB{144} the block being filled; one RATE of the sponge
;   @0x3d0:0x3f5  the exclusive or frame; xor64 pasted at @0x3d0
;   @0x3f8        mlo     message bytes still to come  low byte
;   @0x3f9        mhi     and high byte
;   @0x3fa        msgleft one while either of those is not nought
;   @0x3fb        pad     one until the padding byte has been placed
;   @0x3fc        more    one while another block is wanted
;   @0x3fd        ic      the a hundred and forty four bytes of a block
;   @0x3fe:0x403  t0 t1 e0 t2 t3 e1  the cells the four tests are made through
;   @0x404        last    one if the padding byte was placed in THIS block
;
; WHY THIS ONE IS A FILE OF ITS OWN AND SHA3_256 IS A HEAD OVER keccak/sponge136:
; a rate cannot be a parameter in brainfuck  because every journey the absorb
; makes would then be of a computed length and there is no index to compute one
; from; So there is one sponge per RATE; A padding byte can be a parameter
; because it is one cell of data  so where two functions share a rate they share
; one file and hand it their own byte; The rate 136 is shared by SHA3_256 and
; SHAKE256 and so has a sponge and two heads; THIS rate has exactly one function
; in the whole of FIPS 202  so the sponge and the head are the same file and its
; two constants are written straight into it;
;
; AND THERE IS NO SQUEEZE LOOP HERE for the same reason: twenty eight bytes is
; under one rate  so the digest is the front of the state and is emitted where
; it lies; keccak/sponge136 pays one whole turn of the state to serve a length
; it does not know in advance  and this file does not have to;
;
; THE RATE IS A HUNDRED AND FORTY FOUR and that is exactly EIGHTEEN LANES  so absorbing a
; block is eighteen entries of xor64 rather than a hundred and forty four byte
; exclusive ors; Every rate in the family divides by eight  which is the one
; thing that carries over from one of these files to the next;
;
; AND EVERY OPERAND IS MOVED  never copied: the state lane is replaced by the
; answer and the block is spent  so nothing needs handing back;
;
; THE BLOCK IS FILLED BY A CONVEYOR  because there is no index: a byte always
; enters at the TOP of the block and the block slides down one before the next
; one arrives; So the byte that enters first has slid 143 times when the
; block is full and comes to rest at the bottom  which is where it belongs;
;
; THE PADDING IS FIPS 202's  and the conveyor makes it almost free: when the
; message runs out the next byte to enter is 6  and after that nothing enters at
; all  which leaves noughts behind the conveyor exactly as the rule wants; The
; last byte of the LAST block then gains 128; That byte is either nought or the
; 6 itself  so the addition cannot carry  and the case where the message is a
; whole number of blocks needs no special arm: the padding simply gets a block
; of its own;
;
; ON THE LAST BLOCK AND NOT ON EVERY BLOCK; The block in which the padding byte
; was placed is the last block by definition  so placing it sets a flag and the
; 128 is added under that flag; The rate 136 sponge got this wrong first time
; and only failed once a message was long enough to need two blocks;
;
; A BLOCK IS ABOUT TWO AND A HALF BILLION INSTRUCTIONS  nearly all of it the
; permutation at two thousand four hundred and eighty four million  so nothing
; else in this file is worth optimising until that is;
;
; The length is read into the bottom two cells of the STATE and moved up out of
; it  because a read prologue may hold nothing but commas and steps and the
; state must start at nought; Every distance below was worked out from the map;

; read the message length little endian
  ,>,
